WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:04.650
Monday morning in the business district of
Bamenda.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.120
It's a sad sight: whole neighborhoods of the
biggest city in the region have come to a

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.530
standstill -- most businesses remain closed.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:19.590
Greengrocer Robert isn't opening his shop
today - even though he badly needs to.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:27.370
"It is a very difficult situation but if you
can imagine on a day like this some of us

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.660
we live on a daily bread meaning that today
there is no bread.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:37.980
Today there is no bread but we adapt because
it's a cause that we are fighting for."

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.710
Robert says he hasn't seen any development
in the region -- even though he regularly

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.140
pays his taxes.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:49.310
He and others are protesting by not opening
their businesses and they're also calling

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:53.220
for the release of a number of demonstrators.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.579
In the mostly English-speaking west of Cameroon,
many people feel marginalized.

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:02.989
They feel they've been forgotten by President
Paul Biya and the French-speaking majority

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:05.420
of the country.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.570
In late 2016, lawyers took to the streets
to protest.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:15.160
Teachers soon followed suit - then finally
people from all walks of life.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.570
The authorities responded with a heavy hand.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:22.930
At least six people died and dozens were arrested.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.830
Internet access in the region was blocked
for three months.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:33.260
"We tried to talk to the governor about the
situation, but he didn’t grant us an interview.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:38.119
A government spokesperson told us on the phone
that actions are more important than words

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:40.250
and they are working on a solution.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:45.090
But here most people complain that they don’t
see any serious dialogue.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:50.970
Instead, some people become more radical."

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:55.869
Businesses owned by people who did not take
part in the protest are often the target of

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:58.630
arson attacks.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:02.060
We talks to a young man who wants to remain
anonymous.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.290
He himself was almost arrested.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.960
He wants the region to become independent.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.300
He thinks the use of violence is legitimate,
because he doesn't think the government would

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.380
allow a referendum.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:13.959
"It's a necessary evil.

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:17.680
I wouldn't say setting people's properties
on fire is a good thing.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.810
But it's a necessary evil as of now.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.260
If I have to tell you everything that runs
through my head, I might look like a terrorist to you.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.260
 

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:25.260
But I'm not a terrorist!

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.230
But when you look at the frustration, when
the frustration mounts to a certain extent

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.010
you cannot contain, you become radical.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.010
That's what happens.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:36.650
We are just hoping that sometime soon somebody
will come and say: Here are the guns you need,

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:38.150
take them and fight for your freedom!

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.900
And we will just so do!"

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.200
The mood in the city is tense.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.170
Divisions between radicals and moderates have
widened.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:03:10.739
The Church has tried to mediate -- and is
calling on all parties to engage

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:24.530
in dialogue.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:29.630
Robert the greengrocer is also hoping that
there will be a peaceful resolution, and that

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:31.819
the government finally responds.

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:36.170
Schools have been closed for over a year now
and his kids have been affected.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.510
Robert says the current situation cannot continue.

